{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789303306,"nonce":"0T56DcnMYwMDEVmWpCzV/iWT9fg=","title":"A closure capturing a for-loop variable together with a body local fails with 'subscript get with arity 1'","message":"Reproducer (every mode, including --mode interpreter):\n\n    var keep = []\n    for (round in 0...2) {\n      var n = [round]\n      keep.add(Fn.new { \"%(round) %(n)\" })\n    }\n    for (f in keep) System.print(f.call())\n\nExpected 0 [0] / 1 [1]; actual: Error: unsupported: subscript get with arity 1, pointing at the range in the for header. Capturing only n (nested loops or not) works, and the same shape with a while loop and a manual counter works, as does copying the loop variable into a body local first (var k = round) and capturing k. So the for-loop lowering mishandles a captured loop variable when another captured local shares the body: some slot the loop's iterate/iteratorValue sequence uses is aliased with the boxed upvalue.","files":null}]}